From 18f3a7d5844ccefce4eb240bede139eef0e8a088 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: redC0rvus <111829302+redC0rvus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 01:20:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 12/24] [general] system: seed FPSCR host state on XHostThreads

GPU interrupts and audio callbacks run guest code on XHostThread contexts that never called fpscr.InitHost(). With csr = 0, the first FlushMode/mtfsf write unmasked every host FP exception and an inexact result killed the process (0xC000008F).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/system/xthread.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/system/xthread.cpp b/src/system/xthread.cpp
index 91957d3..cef200d 100644
--- a/src/system/xthread.cpp
+++ b/src/system/xthread.cpp
@@ -1454,6 +1454,11 @@ void XHostThread::Execute() {
   // Let the kernel know we are starting.
   kernel_state_->OnThreadExecute(this);
 
+  // Host threads run guest callbacks (GPU interrupts, audio) on this context.
+  // An unseeded csr (0) would unmask every host FP exception on the first
+  // FlushMode/mtfsf write, and an inexact result then kills the process.
+  thread_state()->context()->fpscr.InitHost();
+
   int ret = host_fn_();
 
   // Exit.
